WEBVTT

00:00:06.375 --> 00:00:10.916
- Hand it over, or I shoot.
- With great-grandpa's musket?

00:00:11.041 --> 00:00:14.000
That thing is over a hundred years old.
It won't even work.

00:00:14.125 --> 00:00:16.000
Shall we put it to the test?

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.083
(All) Gina!

00:00:22.666 --> 00:00:24.208
(Hunter gasps)

00:00:25.958 --> 00:00:29.000
She means it.
And she's very strong for a nun.

00:00:29.125 --> 00:00:31.458
She's not a nun!

00:00:31.583 --> 00:00:33.750
The gold or your daughter?

00:00:33.875 --> 00:00:36.541
You're all family.
Couldn't you just share the gold?

00:00:36.666 --> 00:00:38.958
Cabotos don't share!

00:00:40.458 --> 00:00:42.875
- Sorry, it was just a thought.
- It was a very good one.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.833
Papa, please!

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:51.583
But I am so close.
I cannot lose it now.

00:00:51.708 --> 00:00:56.625
I have been searching forever
in this... sweaty jungle,

00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:03.083
and I am hot and flushed
and-and-and uncomfortable, and...

00:01:10.708 --> 00:01:13.708
Why do I feel so...

00:01:16.333 --> 00:01:17.583
...queasy?

00:01:17.708 --> 00:01:21.208
It's called a hard stare, Mr Hunter.

00:01:21.333 --> 00:01:25.875
And it's for when people have forgotten
their manners and the important things.

00:01:28.041 --> 00:01:31.208
- Yeah...
- Gina's your treasure.

00:01:31.333 --> 00:01:34.000
Don't lose her because of gold.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.583
Gina will steal the gold for herself.

00:01:41.708 --> 00:01:44.458
- Choose the gold!
- You can always get a new daughter.

00:01:44.583 --> 00:01:46.375
Cabotos don't share!

00:01:49.791 --> 00:01:51.875
I'm sorry, Gina.

00:02:01.958 --> 00:02:04.041
All I can say is, er...

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:07.666
- ...boom.
- Boom?

00:02:07.791 --> 00:02:08.750
Boom!

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:20.000
- Oh! (Giggling)
- Huh...

00:02:20.125 --> 00:02:22.125
Oh, dear... What?

00:02:23.458 --> 00:02:26.458
- No, no, no!
- Papa!

00:02:27.208 --> 00:02:29.375
Here. Here...

00:02:36.125 --> 00:02:38.208
You're free.

00:02:38.333 --> 00:02:40.333
We are free.

00:02:58.791 --> 00:03:03.083
Go... and find your Aunt Lucy.

00:03:03.208 --> 00:03:06.083
You're not coming, Mr Hunter?

00:03:07.833 --> 00:03:09.833
Mr Paddington, um...

00:03:11.041 --> 00:03:14.041
...I've got all the treasure I need.

00:03:17.375 --> 00:03:19.041
Thank you, Mr Hunter.

00:03:20.625 --> 00:03:23.791
Oh, no... thank you.

00:03:26.083 --> 00:03:27.500
Mmm...

00:03:42.333 --> 00:03:46.000
Um... I'll just try that again.

00:03:46.916 --> 00:03:48.333
(Blows)

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:57.750
- (Low rumbling)
- Huh?

00:03:59.416 --> 00:04:02.750
- (Mrs Bird) What's happening?
- (Mrs Brown) Whoa!

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:06.791
- (Mrs Bird) It's opening! It's opening!
- What's happening? Oh, my goodness!

00:04:06.916 --> 00:04:09.000
(Mrs Bird) Back! Back!

00:04:25.791 --> 00:04:28.208
(Mrs Bird) Oh! Oh, my...

00:04:28.333 --> 00:04:30.666
- Oh, it's the...
- It's... it's from the book, the weird...

00:04:30.791 --> 00:04:33.875
- Yes, the "Espiritus del Bosque".
- (Judy) The forest spirits...

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.833
- (Mrs Brown) Yes.
- (Judy) They're real.

00:04:35.958 --> 00:04:37.625
Oh!

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:40.375
- (Roaring)
- Oh!

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:42.041
They don't sound friendly.

00:04:43.791 --> 00:04:46.041
Quite the opposite, Mr Brown.

00:04:46.916 --> 00:04:49.708
That was my bear name.

00:04:50.458 --> 00:04:52.041
Oh...

00:04:54.375 --> 00:04:57.625
- They want us to go inside.
- Really?

00:04:58.458 --> 00:05:01.125
Thank you. Afternoon.

00:05:02.333 --> 00:05:04.166
Thank you so much.

